+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same directory is published a second time in a machine-readable form, which carries every veterinarian and their specialties in one response rather than a page at a time `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+Either form can be narrowed to a single specialty named in the request. The reader then sees only the veterinarians holding that specialty, matched on the whole specialty name and disregarding letter case, so part of a name matches nothing. A specialty no veterinarian holds narrows the directory to an empty list rather than reporting a failure, and naming no specialty leaves the directory exactly as it was. Moving between pages of a narrowed directory keeps the narrowing `[REQ-VET-004]`. Choosing the specialty is asked for in the request; neither form gains a control on the page for picking one.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the machine-readable directory is requested, then every veterinarian and their specialties come back in one response.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a specialty some veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened naming it, then only those veterinarians are listed, still a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a specialty some veterinarians hold, when the machine-readable directory is requested naming it, then only those veterinarians come back.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a named specialty differing from the held specialty only by letter case, when either form is requested, then it matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given only part of a specialty's name, when either form is requested, then no veterinarian matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when either form is requested, then the directory comes back in its normal shape with an empty list, not as a failure.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a narrowed directory spanning more than one page, when the reader moves to another page, then the narrowing still holds.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a specialty named as blank or as spaces alone, when either form is requested, then the directory comes back as though none had been named.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given no specialty named, when either form is requested, then the directory is exactly what it was before narrowing existed.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. A named specialty carrying leading or trailing spaces narrows the same way as the same name without them, matching the convention `REQ-OWN-002` sets for owner search.
+3. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears in the unnarrowed directory and in no narrowed one.
 
